This project is a premium, ultra-luxury healthcare website for "SR³ ENT & SURGICAL CENTRE". The stack is React (Vite) + Tailwind CSS + Framer Motion (for animations) + Lucide React (for icons).

Design System, Theming & Branding:

Brand Alignment: The UI must complement the official circular logo, which features a dark background, crisp white text, and vibrant yellow/gold medical iconography (ENT head profile and surgeon).

Colors: Use a deep dark navy/charcoal (e.g., #1A1B26 or #0A192F) derived from the logo's background for dark sections and footers. Use crisp white and soft clinical gray for content backgrounds. Use the distinct vibrant yellow/gold from the logo's accent graphics for primary buttons, active tabs, and CTAs to create strong visual consistency.

Typography: Use an elegant, distinguished serif font for all headings, section titles, and doctor names. Use a clean, modern sans-serif for body text, paragraphs, and medical qualifications.

UI/UX Vibe: The site must look like a world-class international private clinic—clean, spacious, and trust-inspiring. Use glassmorphism for the navbar and soft shadows for doctor profile cards. Iconography across the site (via Lucide React) should be clean and line-based to match the logo's aesthetic.

Coding Conventions:

Keep components modular within the src/components/ directory.

Ensure all layouts are strictly mobile-responsive using Tailwind utility classes.

All clinic data (doctors, services, contact info) should be cleanly hardcoded within the frontend components. No backend or external database connection is required.

Maintain smooth, premium fade-in animations on scroll and subtle hover states (like slightly lifting cards) across the app.